<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Noreia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Noreia was the chief town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norici">Norici</a> in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, mentioned by Roman writers but never firmly located. Near it the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri">Cimbri</a> defeated a Roman army under Gnaeus Papirius Carbo in 113 BCE, and Caesar records that the Boii besieged it before joining the Helvetii. It is generally sought in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noreia.jpg" alt="Noreia" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Atlas of Ancient and Classical Geography, 1907 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Noricum_1907.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
